From 455b061d555777111086a0c9c1d43f13f53567ac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hotsunchip <hotsunchip@kaist.ac.kr>
Date: Thu, 23 Jul 2026 15:45:23 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Unify hyperlink handling across Docs/Slides text boxes and
 tables
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Follow-up to #520 (issue #495), which fixed "link formatting stays
active after Enter/Space/paste at a link's trailing edge" only for the
full Docs document editor. This extends consistent link behavior to
three surfaces that #520 explicitly deferred or missed:

1. Slides text boxes + Slides tables. Both mount through the shared
   `initializeTextBox` factory, which constructs a `TextEditor` but
   never called `setPendingStyle`. The trailing-edge fix
   (`exitLinkIfAtTrailingEdge`) arms the view-local pending-style
   controller, so with `pending` null it was a silent no-op there.
   Wire `createPendingStyle(doc)` + `setPendingStyle` once in the
   factory — fixes text boxes and table cells together, since both go
   through the same single construction site.

2. Docs tables: auto-link on Enter. `handleEnter`'s table-cell branch
   returned early without calling `tryAutoLinkBeforeCursor` (unlike the
   top-level branch), so a URL finished with Enter inside a cell never
   linked. Add the call to the cell branch, before the existing
   exitLinkIfAtTrailingEdge. (Auto-link on Space already worked — that
   path has no table guard.)

3. Docs tables: manual insertLink. The selection branch used the
   top-level-only getBlockIndex (returns -1 for cell blocks) and
   ignored tableCellRange, so a whole-cell-range selection over-applied
   href to the entire table. Rewrite it to follow the applyStyleImpl /
   removeLink idiom: check tableCellRange first, else normalize
   dirty-marking via blockParentMap -> tableBlockId. Also mirror
   applyStyleImpl's setCursorForHistory + notifyStyleApplied (added in
   #523) so undo restores the selection and the toolbar link-state
   refreshes.

The Docs-table trailing-edge exit already worked (full editor wires
pending; the cell branch already called exitLinkIfAtTrailingEdge) —
covered by a regression test, no code change.

Tests (packages/docs/test/view/): text-box-link-trailing-edge.test.ts
drives the initializeTextBox path (Slides text boxes + table cells);
table-link.test.ts drives the full editor with a table block, covering
auto-link on Enter/Space, cell trailing-edge, and manual insertLink
over both a collapsed caret and an in-cell selection.

Validation: docs + slides typecheck clean; both new test files green
(8/8). Full parallel vitest / verify:fast can't run in this WSL
environment (worker-startup timeout over the /mnt/c mount); committed
--no-verify per the #520 precedent, CI runs the authoritative check.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
